===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|brere}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{m|ang|brēr}}, {{m|ang|brǣr||briar; bramble}}, possibly ultimately from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*wert-||to twist, turn}}. Compare Icelandic {{m|is|brörr||briar}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# Any of many plants with thorny stems growing in dense clusters, such as many in the ''[[Rosa]], [[Rubus]]'', and ''[[Smilax]]'' genera.
# {{lb|en|figurative}} Anything sharp or unpleasant to the feelings.
#* {{rfdate|}} {{w|Cowper}}
#*: The thorns and '''briers''' of reproof.

